                                                     <p  class="paragraph">When our walk comes to an end, we realize this route won’t ever be complete. New names still appear on the map of Lviv mathematicians, lost graves are found, archival documents reveal new biographies, and relatives send photographs and family stories.&nbsp;</p>
                                                     <p  class="paragraph">Maybe the most important thing in this project isn’t the QR codes. They only help make visible history that could have stayed buried under a layer of moss forever, like Zygmunt Janiszewski’s gravestone. In truth, this project is about returning the memory — because behind every QR code, there are years of work in the archives, serendipitous finds, international acquaintances, and dozens of people who are helping to bring the history of science in Lviv back to life.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
